WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:05.750
A two-hundred-forty-dollar return hits the
hard gate, and waits for a human.

00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:11.230
Support tickets are judgment work with
money attached,

00:00:11.230 --> 00:00:14.200
and every refund must trace back to
policy.

00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:20.208
The E-commerce Support and Returns Copilot
verifies the order,

00:00:20.208 --> 00:00:23.549
applies the return policy
deterministically,

00:00:23.549 --> 00:00:25.675
and escalates large refunds.

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:31.199
The model reads the ticket and drafts the
reply. Code verifies,

00:00:31.199 --> 00:00:34.550
decides — and a human gates the big
refunds.

00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:40.584
A deterministic policy engine decides
eligibility and amounts.

00:00:40.584 --> 00:00:43.700
The model only drafts the explanation.

00:00:44.500 --> 00:00:47.687
Refunds above a cap can't be
auto-approved.

00:00:47.687 --> 00:00:50.800
It's enforced at the database write layer.

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:56.546
A twenty-two-technique injection corpus
runs before any worker,

00:00:56.546 --> 00:00:59.000
with a hundred percent block rate.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:02.427
On thirty-six synthetic tickets,

00:01:02.427 --> 00:01:06.219
the pipeline resolves a hundred percent
correctly.

00:01:06.219 --> 00:01:08.950
A single bare prompt manages eleven.

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:15.475
Want this adapted to your own store? Get
in touch at kaarstenanderson.com.
